@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/messages/[message_uuid]/actions/unstar/invoke
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "WorkspaceMessageController\nRestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\ncanonical lines + brackets" as DB
queue "Transactional outbox\n+ Typed tasks" as Outbox
participant "Worker scope=user-message\nlease + fencing" as Worker
database "Ready projections\nThe container is tied up ." as Projection
database "The public events repository" as Events
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as Dispatcher
actor "The client . WebSocket" as WS
Client -> API: POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/messages/{message_uuid}/actions/unstar/invoke
API -> DB: resolve public placement; check active membership + generation
API -> DB: placement STATE.starred=false + immutable outbox event
DB --> API: The transaction is recorded
API --> Client: A successful public response
DB ->> Outbox: the event that was recorded
Outbox ->> Worker: immutable read_counters(outbox_event_uuid,\nproject+user+placement); without coalescing
Worker -> Worker: One fenced owner exact user-message scope
Worker -> Projection: presenting a message to the current user
Worker -> Events: message.updated current user\natomically in one. DB transaction with a projection
Events ->> Dispatcher: fixed ready line
Dispatcher ->> WS: I 'm going to send / repeat / reproduce
note over API,Worker
  Topic lock Not used. Retry/backoff, DLQ/reaper - They 're compulsory ..
end note
@enduml
